<h2>The challenge</h2><p>Operational teams need consistent answers from data originating across multiple systems. Missing records, changing upstream feeds, and ambiguous metric definitions can undermine trust even when dashboards look polished.</p>
<h2>Technical approach</h2><ul><li>Consolidate upstream sources and transform them in a cloud data warehouse.</li><li>Formalize business definitions and implement checks that help catch coverage or quality regressions.</li><li>Expose decision-ready metrics through analytics products and purpose-built interfaces.</li><li>Design reporting and user experiences around the action a business stakeholder needs to take.</li></ul>
<h2>The judgment behind the work</h2><p>The difficult judgment is often about reliability: choosing the right source, deciding which discrepancies require escalation, and making uncertainty visible rather than letting it disappear inside a dashboard.</p>
<div class="callout">Why this project is here: it illustrates a combination of modeling judgment, engineering tradeoffs, and attention to the decisions the system supports—not a claim of performance without evidence.</div>
<h2>Evidence to add</h2><p>Approved screenshots, before-and-after reliability measures, and anonymized metric examples can be incorporated after disclosure review.</p>
